Iranian students are ready to die for their country's nuclear program.
They created a vivid Shield
Several Hundred undergraduates have created a living shank around a nuclear facility in Iran.
With their gesture, they want to express support for their country's nuclear program ahead of a possible Israeli attack.
At noon, the students commuted in front of the object on Tuesday and then chanted the deaths of the U.S. and Israel.
Several Hundred university students in Isfahan, Iran's Isfahan, on Tuesday, formed a living shield around the Isfahan's Nuclear Technology Center where uranium is being processed.
This makes it clear that they are ready to defend their country's nuclear program with their own lives.
The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) said in a recent report that Iran did not seem to have ceased to strive for a nuclear weapon.
A possible attack on Iranian nuclear facilities is being talked about in Israel.
At noon at noon before entering the Isfahan's nuclear facility, the students prayed and then chanted the deaths of America and Israel.
In the event of an attack designed to cripple an Iranian nuclear program as much as possible as much as possible, according to the Israeli press, in addition to the Isfahan center, the target would also include a Natanz facility in which uranium is enriched.
Obese child's diet: does not have breakfast and sausage dinner
More than a one-thousand children aged between 9 and 13 have overweight problems, with an overgive weight of 9 per cent of schoolchildren and obsessive 5 per cent of children.
Obese children usually come from unhealthy-style families, according to current research.
It is once again shown how important it is for the healthy development of a person in the environment in which he grows, and the patterns with which he is surrounded.
For example, sausceptible sausages appear on the tables of obese children by up to half more often than in the families of children with normal weight.
Fried fries for dinner the day before the research associated with an awareness-raising event called Obesity, more than 19 per cent of obsessive.
There is also no habit of playing sports in fat families, which, of course, applies to most families of today’s schoolchildren – only 15 percent of children responded that their parents find time for active exercise at least once a week.
Exploration among 900 children
The survey was carried out at the end of the last school year and was attended by almost 900 children from elementary schools from all over the Czech Republic.
It was the second year of the Obesity event is not a coincidence, which is supported by the General Health Insurer and Uniliver.
So far, more than 12,000 schoolchildren from grades 4-8 have participated in the project.
Proper eating and enough exercise in the family is one of the defining factors that causes a dramatically increasing number of overweight or even obeste.
"Only half of those surveyed, for example, stated that they eat five times a day in breakfast-shougar-snack-summer-summer-summer mode, which is one of the basic presumptuous prerequisites for proper nutrition," is one of the results of the survey.
Without breakfast and in the evening sausage
Experts point out that relative details are also important for healthy development, such as the regular time of single-family breakfasts.
At the same time, only 23 percent of families of schoolchildren eat breakfast in the Czech Republic at the same time.
In the majority of our families, everyone eats alone.
And the worst thing was to find out that in a ten-and-a-halg of a household doesn't eat breakfast at all.
Even breakfast is the basis of a proper daily diet.
The questionnaire showed that unhealthy fries are consumed much more often in the families of obese children.
Nearly everyone - regardless of the weight - drinks sweet lemonade every day (70 per cent).
Although more than 40 percent of the children surveyed regularly do sports, the result for their parents was less than half - 15 per cent.
Build down your diet
Another part of the survey made it possible to compute for selected children (204 boys and 172 girls from 13 schools) to build their own diet according to their own taste and their own opinion.
"Different preferences of Czech children between the ages of 12 and 15 in terms of a healthy diet are far from an ideal."
Among their favorite dishes there is a lot of floury, fleshy and sweet dishes.
"In particular, the great popularity of sweet lemonades is an alarming thing," according to a final survey report.
Pasta prevailed for lunch as the main dish just above the poultry.
However, children practically did not want legumes at all, and the popularity of fish and mid-summer vegetable dishes is also low.
Inclination to health
At the same time, the survey showed that children are willing to adjust their eating habits if they get the right information.
"The control group of survey participants, who completed the questionnaire after the end of the awareness-raising lecture Obesity is not a coincidence, in a number of cases there has been a significant shift of preferences towards the principles of a healthy diet," according to the results of the project.
It has been noticeable, for example, in sweet lemonades, where more children would begin to prefer ordinary water.
Babies also ticked poultry and fish as the main meal of the day much more often in the questionnaire, limiting sweet foods and dumplings.
Stylist must also be a good psychologist, professes
In an introductory article about how stylists are taught, I complained a little that there was already a lot in the opening hours.
I didn’t know what was going to happen.
Lectures of three professionals from the industry, dressing problematic characters and a seminar on how it goes on set.
And it's going to get any worse.
The closer to the final exam, the more information and practical tasks await us.
And even though the course takes place every Sabbath and Sunday every Saturday, it is really "stamped".
This time we were discussing with director Alice (there is not the only boy in the course), how to dress a woman who does not have a perfectly sy symmetrical figure.
These are the vast majority.
Someone's got a short neck, someone has a boy's figure without proper crooks, and someone is overweight again.
The stylist needs to know how to visually soften wide shoulders, lengthen the neck or supply the necessary curves.
We were given tips on how with a Jennifer Lopez-type woman, i.e. larger breasts and hips and a narrow waist, emphasizing the physicist and at the same time don’t dress a woman too provocatively.
If, for example, there is the difference between the waist and the hips that the skirt or pants really do not fit, then it pays to be sewn at at least one such piece.
You won’t feel sorry, because perfectly-fitting clothes are priceless.
You will feel much better in a tailbone skirt rather than one that is constantly shifting, elevating, staying at the waist and the like.
In turn, a boy's character can afford to wear clothes with creases, applications, embroideries or hikes.
Of course there are a lot of such information and types of characters, so I'm glad I've got a whole week to sort out all the information in my head.
And I'm still afraid that given the assigned homework, it's.
Each of the curiosities was given an assigned celebrity, who is supposed to come up with two outfits: a day and an evening.
We need to take into account the up-to-date appearance, the fashionable style of the personality and the type of figure.
I'll "Dress" Miranda Kerr, you may know her from Victoria's Secret campaigns.
In the spirit of cheering, for me personally definitely better than Britney Spears, Christina Aguiler, who has recently gained perhaps a hundred kilos lately (please take into account exaggeration) or threshing Selena Gomez.
We have to cut the suits out of magazines or search on the Internet and print and then process it graphically.
Moodboard, as they are called the whole result, will then also express our personal style and relationship to the graphic rendition.
It is also important to think about the graphic side of styling.
The stylist does not only dress physically, but also creates, for example, so-called product pages in magazines (for specific assignments, such as trendy handbags, coats, etc.).
Stylista and designer Mario Kameník told us about it.
It wasn't until Sunday.
Stylist must have a general overview
Saturday's lecture charged with information about the types of characters was diversified by three guests in the field.
Stylist Honza Pokorný, fashion designer Jakub Polanka and fashion photographer Ben Renč.
Jakub reminded us that fashion is an Illuminent and the stylist should be able to take advantage of it.
And a skilful stylist knows how to work with one piece of clothing in different ways.
The variability is crucial in this case.
For example, such trench coat (or if you originally want trenchcoat) can be worn classically through jeans and a T-shirt as a cloak, but you can also put it on a bare-dyed body, put shoes on a hemp and shoot like a dress.
Or it is enough just to roll up the sleeves or collars and immediately the whole look looks different.
"Figuse it with it," he stressed.
However, I appreciated the following advice: "To work you need to know the rules perfectly."
"Then you can start violating them," Jacob said.
Finally it is clear to me why we grunt down all these propositions, what to combine with what to combine, for what, why, when even in fashion magazines we sometimes sometimes see something else.
Don’t even mention the paradoes.
Thanks to photographer Ben, I already know that the stylist has to have a lot more variants of clothing ready than how many can be photographed.
So with a fashion story, which will have ten sides (i.e. ten outfits), I have to be ready to "cover" for at least fifteen.
And also the fact that in the photo of clothes it looks and works in combination with other pieces sometimes completely different than in reality.
So we have to take this into account when creating an outfit.
Honza Pokorný confirmed that image and style sometimes make up to half of the success.
Just take a look at Madonna, who isn't exactly a miraculous singer, but image and marketing have made her a world-leading star.
So far in the Czech Republic, the approach to the use of stylista services is rather cold.
Familiar cheeks sometimes consider it useless (it is enough that I can do something, what I look like is secondary).
And if someone already let us create styling from us, then we have to reckon that they are most likely to dictulate a completely different (smaller) size than he really has.
Then all we have to do is googled and find out if the tabloids didn't write about the fact that the celebrity blunted/moved and so on.
Honza and Mario on Sunday told us that it is not enough for the stylist to orient himself in fashion and to be able to put together an outfit.
During his work he primarily communicates with the people he dresses, so it is also important to be a good psychologist.
Being able to estimate people, don't pandemic, to stand up for your point of view.
"When a manager orders you to cut her through the closet and rebuild it with nice pieces, you can't throw her the whole closet and say, for God's sake, that's terrifying."
"Find at least a few things that you compliment and recommend what they can be worn for," Mario says.
He also specifically showed us what the so-so-called "sflat bag" must contain.
It's the one that you turn on around the waist and you've got all the necessary proprieties.
In addition to bright things such as scisssors, hair rollers or closing pins, there are also silon nit (with it the stylist helps himself to shoot products such as handbags or hats), special clicards, through which we fasten our clothes in the back, if there is a larger (an incank or other clamp are not permissible, they would devadu devadue the garment).
In order not only to listen, but also to practically try something, we have learned how to properly salute shoes.
Even when photographing in the studio, where there is a flat surface, the sole could be damaged, i.e. outdoor.
So we glued and glued.
Scisssors can't even be touched, so they don't get damaged.
It really requires dexterity.
Mario delighted me when he complied my creation unreserved.
This skill is really not my cruciate friend.
That's just a tiny fraction of what we've listened to on the second weekend's sequel.
It is becoming more and more clear to me that devoting yourself to styling on a professional level really isn't a walk through a rose-tinted orchard, no matter who knows what they want.
In Need for Speed: The Run is racing across America.
Reviews
Originally a carefree cavalry, due to a streuger of completely useless sloppy mistakes, turns into a routine morning journey on a shift.
Although the ambition was largely fulfilled, it is of no use when no one clearly wanted to do anything extra.
A new episode subtitled The Run aroused high anticipations prior to the release.
He vowed to move the years-long racing series Need for Speed in a new direction again, appearing as a play-and-monetary game that might not have to be in the genre of action-packed racing.
We were also curious to see how the inserted passages would turn out, in which the main hero will get out of the car and go on foot.
As is customary with the NFS franchise, a lot is a little bit different than we expected.
These are potentially decent arcade races, but the whole drags down a few unnecessary festivities that have been appearing in the series for more or less for several years.
In fact, these are not mistakes, but rather a manifestation of some incomprehensible laziness of the developers.
The adventure starts very well.
You're put into a story whose main hero Jack has certain problems of a personal character and as a solution is offered participation in an illicit race across the America.
Behind the wheel you will sit on the west coast of San Francisco and your task is to arrive first in New York.
The idea entails a few interesting elements.
The route is divided into ten stages, as well as into more than fifty races.
From this it follows that each race rides on a different track and these stages are planted in different, sufficiently different and interesting environments.
You don’t have a moment that the game offers the same thing all the time.
In addition, some of the environments are very handsome to look at, even though the technical level of graphics corresponds to the previous parts of the series.
So it's nothing world-renowned.
But a ride across the desert, an autumnal landscape or high in snow-capped mountains looks visually very enjoyable.
In addition, from time to time the race is diversched by an uncharacteristic element.
In the desert, for example, you bring yourself into a sandstorm, which greatly reduces visibility.
On the other hand, you have to be careful in the mountains so you don’t have an avalanche.
In addition, individual races are set quite well behind each other.
There are only a few types, but that's enough.
For a while you try to overtake the required number of competitors (esseually a classic race), then you're catching the time (a classic duel with shanks) and then a duel with a single opponent awaits you.
From time to time, even the police get involved, who make all your efforts even more uncomfortable.
A novelty is the passages outside the wagon.
Rather, it is just such an interactive animation, when Jack usually flees in front of someone, and you have to help them by pressing the right buttons in the right moments.
It's nothing complicated.
Surprisingly, there are much fewer of these passages in the game than you would expect (specifically, perhaps only three).
As a result, however, it is to the benefit of the matter, because this element has no chance to become annoying and, in the context of the above, it ranks among the elements that diversify the game.
The journey model follows in the footsteps of the previous parts.
This means that it’s definitely nobody anymore, but it can’t be said to be a negative.
If you are looking for a realistic simulation, you will have to look somewhere else.
But a more action-conceived racing the local riding model still suits quite well, even though we would be able to find a better one in the competition.
That's why everything in perfect order.
However, the problems begin to appear after a while.
Contrary to the driving model, the collide model is no longer very right.
We don’t expect a game of this type to calculate complex deformations and collisions, but if you don’t have the slightest idea how your car behaves, then it’s probably not all right.
Typically, when overtaking or passing cars in normal traffic, you sometimes only slightly quench each other, but at other times in an almost-identical situation, your car will end up in wild pirouettes.
Or even an intruder.
Thanks to the reboot system, it doesn’t particularly matter, but it upsets you reliably.
Reboots are handled in such a way that if you smashed or ride far outside the track, the game will throw you back to the last clue on the track.
Reboots are only five available in each race.
When you exhaust them, you have to start the race again from the beginning.
So it's more of an attire in case something doesn't go wrong rather than relying on them.
But sometimes even the reboots do not help, they will only be solved by the need to learn a given section of the race by merchandise.
The great ailcle of the game is that the same things often happen in the same places.
For example, it is necessary to go through some curves in a specific way, otherwise you simply do not fit into them.
At other times you will always meet "civilian" cars at a given place in the same configuancy, whether you arrive there first, fifth, five seconds earlier or a minute later.
This is particularly annoyed in situations when you can see how between the two oncoming cars the competitor drives in front of you lightly, while when you get there, there are already cars in such a position that you have to detour or brake them.
It doesn’t matter when you reach them, because it is “calculbed” in such a way that the situation always occurs just in front of your nose.
Competitors also have another advantage.
During the whole time of playing, you will come across a few places where, again regardless of the time, the same competitor in the same place.
It cuts the most at the end of the game on a long bridge, where you go in the opposite direction.
An adversary in front of you clearly has to get there at any cost.
When he rides in front of you deteriorates the overview of oncoming cars, so at first you probably squander a few times.
It is possible to misunderstood the intent to make the game suspensive and more adrenaline-fuelled, but the execution is so obvious that it reliably reliably distaste you.
And it is a pity, because despite a simple driving model, gaming is fun and in some places so action that sometimes you literally don't have time to watch where it flies.
And it doesn’t really matter whether it’s merit of a concept with fifty unique tracks, raceshitting so that boredom doesn’t have a chance or anything else.
An unconventional idea to change cars during races.
You have to pay attention to gasoline on the roads, because that’s where you can change the car, even though in the vast majority of cases you can make do with what you currently have.
Cars are categorized into three categories.
Athletes are suitable for urban areas, strong American breakers on flat highways and exotic supersports for technical driving, for example along winding mountain paths.
With the main story mode goes hand-in-in-hole mode, which are races in individual locations that you know from the story.
Here you earn not only medals, but experiential points into your profile, which is common to the challenges and the story.
Various objects are unlocked for gaining a higher-level driver: starting with cars and ending with backgrounds for the profile.
At the same time, it is again connected to the online Autolog feature, which, among other things, compares your achieved results with other gamblers and provides other community features.
One of the other hard-and-understood crannies is the situation from the last race in the story.
With your car you can get to the subway tunnel, where you're chasing it in the dark on the tracks (albehind).
On the tachometer you are flashing the numbers between 150 and 200 km/h (yet), and a subway entanglement comes in from the back and uncompromisingly unscrew.
In the newsroom we will probably still have a discussion for a few more days about whether no one really thought a little bit about the creation of the game, or whether the authors consider us really such a big jerk.
The technical aspect of the game is nothing special, but at least the overall visual impression is in most cases very pleasant and in a few cases even great.
It frustrates in such a way that in some more tensile moments the imaging decreases, in some cases quite tragically.
However, it mainly concerns crashers with a larger number of attendees, when smooth photography would no longer be of no use to you.
The sound side is fine and the soundtrack is a matter of taste.
In an intriguing effort to please the widest possible scale of a rather younger audience, a soundtrack from the "either dog of another village" was created, but it can be assumed that in order to listen to the music, someone will probably not just buy the game.
The overall impliance of Need for Speed: The Run is very embarrassing.
If the game was avoided completely unnecessary mistakes, then we wouldn't be afraid to say that The Run is the best part of NFS in the last few years.
That’s how the game works unfinished.
It's definitely good fun, but be prepared for the fact that mistakes will splinter into your eyes with the power of airport reflectors.
Singing choirs UK will be performed at a concert of Velvet Students
For the third time, Festa Academico’s Fensta Academia also offers a combination of the celebration of International Student Day and the anniversary of the Velvet Revolution with a musical experience.
Twenty high school and university choir.
The main center of gravity of the festival is two concerts held on November 17.
"Charle university has a big share in the festival."
"Between the participating choir there is the Choir of the Pedagogical Faculties and the Faculties of the Humanities, the Recreator Václav Hampl will sit in the festival committee," said Jakub Čaloun, head of the organizing team.
The culmination of the whole festival is a freely accessible concert of high school choirs, which will take place on November 17 at 14 o'clock in front of the National Technical Librarian in Dejvice.
On the program is the composition of the important Czech jazzman Karel Růžička Celebration Jazz Mass.
In the evening there will be a concert "Students of Velvet" in the ceremonial premises of the National House in Vinohrady, where university choir choirs, including choir choirs of Charles University, will take place.
Festa Academica aims not only to glouously gloomily Celebrate the International Student Day and commemorate the 22nd Anniversaries of the Velvet Revolution, but also to present choral music to the public at the highest level and develop the creative cooperation of young people.
The main organizer is the Union of Czech choirs in cooperation with Jan Kepler Gymnasium.
Bohuslav Svoboda, the mayor of the Capital City of Prague and the Rector of the Charles University Václav Hampl took over the accusation.
The festival will take place from November 16 to 20 in Prague and Pardubice.
In addition to ceremonial concerts, the schedule also offers a wide range of musical gatherings, student happenings, matina and other shows.
Detailed information can be found by those interested on the festival's website www.festaacademica.cz
Exemption of the EU Vitern:
The Czechs have a reputation as negativists and Euroskeptics
"The Lisbon treaty severely eroded the balance between institutions."
"I didn't expect it to be such a hard war."
"It will take five, six years before the situation stabilizes a little, calms down and before all the players get accustomed to their new roles," Milena Vicenová, the Czech ambassador to the European Union, began her lecture at the Faculty of Law.
To the extent to which her motto "Comprehensibly and versatious about Europe", she pointed out already in the first part of the lecture, when she managed to describe individual EU institutions and their relations in such a clear and comprehensible manner that a number of lecturers from the Faculty of Law of the Charles University could envied it.
Vicenová also complimented the work of the new Permanent President of the European Council Herman Van Rompuy:
"At first there was a critique that he was bleachoy, that he was a grey clerk, that he couldn't fulfill any role, and I have to say that everyone took a breath away, that he handled the role excellently."
“It is a person who knows how to listen to twenty-seven Member States, communicate excellently with them and has a clear vision of where the European Union should go.”
She then explained the new post of high-profile for foreign affairs and security policy in the answer: "Who's the European Union? Which telephone number am I supposed to come to call?" that is as an important step towards the unification and greater readability of EU policy towards countries such as China or India.
No one wants us to ban cheese
Vicenová also dealt with the agenda that the European Council lived, lives and will live in the near future.
Last year's Czech Presidency described it as a success.
The Czechs dealt with the incoming financial crisis, solved the gas crisis or organized a summit for the Eastern Partnership.
At this time, the fall of the government called it a big negative, which severely badly harmed the Czech Republic.
At the same time, the Czech representation in the EU is very busy at the moment.
In the words of the ex-grandmother, the "fect frmol" was not only the presidency, but also the subsequent financial crisis, which is still being dealt with to this day.
In addition, a new seven-year Union budget has yet to be approved, which is very complicated due to the current economic situation.
Whether the budget will be slimmer and austere, which sectors will take precedence, which countries will be promoted more and which less, it is all on the agenda of future negotiations.
The ex-gruator also recalled her main slogans, with which she came to Brussels: "Intelligibly".
"I really don't like nasty abbreviations, foreign words, defamation that no one understands.
"How is a citizen supposed to understand that curvanized or round cucumber cucumbers are not really invented in Brussels, bananas of different sizes, or that someone really has to forbade us to be banning cheese.".
It also wants to make a better use of the EU environment and get more Czechs into the European institutions.
Multi-Speaping Europe awaits us
According to the ex-grandmother, the Czechs have a reputation for Eurosceptics and people who pay attention to the negative ones rather than the positive aspects of the matter.
In addition, it regrets the low representation of Czechs in the European institutions.
According to her, a number of guiding factors, such as the modesty of our candidates, their inability to write motivational letters, as well as low support from the Czech side.
In Addition to the successful Czech Presidency, it emphasized the strength and cooperation of the Visegrad Four.
"Believe me, when a Pole and a Hungarian man comes to see me, the Frenchman next to me will say, "Hey, what are you going to meet there, what's your Visegrad Four?" and he doesn't even look so excited about it."
In the future, according to Vicenová, the Union is mainly awaiting new harsh rules for the budgetary policies of the Member States.
As a very real, he perceives the concept of a two-speaking, if not multi-spoke Europe rather than a new "European federation."
"We have eurozone countries and non-eurozone countries here."
"We have the Schengen area, we already have an institute of enhanced cooperation."
"For the very first time it was said to cooperate only the countries they wanted and those they do not want to stand nearby."
"It's going to be more institutes, and it's going to be a strongly two-speciesty Europe," Vicenová said.
In this respect, it also appreciated the role of the Czech Republic and Herman Van Rompuy in promoting the principle, according to which all topics that have an impact on the whole Union should be debated among all Member States, not only between euro area countries.
Brand story :
Innovator IBM begins the second century of its existence
If someone was looking for a word that would most accurately express IBM's strategy, it would probably have been "Long-goodness".
For the general public, IBM is a symbol of the technological revolution, it has been perceived as a very contemporary company, and yet a hundred years have passed since its inception.
The basis of this longevity was founded by the first head of the company, visionary Thomas J. Watson Sr.
He already conceded the motto that a number of world problems can easily be solved if people are willing to think.
His "Think!" slogan thus became an imprint, around which will unfold the life of the future giant (and the name of an in-main magazine, which began to be published as early as 1935).
It was also the basis of Watson's well-developed corporate culture.
“For us IBM, long-term thinking means a continuous movement towards the future.
IBM has survived and thwarted a hundred years due to the fact that it remained faithful to its basic values and was not afraid to change everything else.
This has allowed us to transform technology, business and society during our first centuries.
We hope to be able to achieve even more in the second Hundred,” commented the company’s current company’s director, Samuel J. Palmisano.
Elaborated system
Watson in the 1930s approached the care of its employees similarly as an entrepreneur Bat'a in the Czech Republic - people from IBM as one of the first U.S. employees had paid leave, insurance from the employer plus an elegant employee uniform and an elaborate system for the remuneration of the best inventors and merchants.
For a long time, IBM has an equally sophisticated relationship with the customer.
From the very beginning, the company was ingeniable in mining talent - as one of the world's first firms, it abolished any discrimination so it could choose.
Pursued by the anti-disciprimination strategy, the current plan is that Palmisan at the head of IBM will be replaced next year by a Virginia Rometta woman.
She has been working at IBM for thirty years, so far she holds the position of sales chief, marketing and strategy.
In recent years, IBM has been making so-called jams, on-line brainstorms, from which many future strategies and innovations arise.
It is not surprising that there are enough ideas - almost half a million people work in the company.
Institutions with a good name
A firm position in the business is ensured by its strong internal and external image.
"Since the beginning, IBM had the concept of an institution rather than just a tech firm," said Economist at the Harvard Business School and the book's author Rosabeth Moss Kanter.
"IBM isn't a technology firm, it's a company that helps solve business problems using technology," added George Colony of Forrester Research.
As the company itself says, there is the only difference between going into the market and creating the market.
According to IBM - or "Great Blue", as it is famously nicknamed because of its logo in the United States - grew into one of the world's largest companies in a hundred years.
It is probably the most versatile technology company - it develops hardware and software, infrasuuction, hosting and consulting services in a variety of products from servers to nanotechnology.
It holds the most patents of any U.S. technology company and five of its employees have won the Nobel Prize.
Its inventions include an ATM, a payment card, a financial swap, a barcode or a franchise.
This year, IBM with about $220 billion became the second-largest technology company according to market capitalization (the first is Apple), when it overtook Microsoft for the first time since 1996.
Looking ahead
Not all products and innovations hit the tastes of customers and times - for example, IBM did not make a bet on its own OS/2 operating system, on-line services Prodigy or IBM PCjr computers.
"If your business is built on moving forward, you can't emotionally tie yourself to the past," Samuel J. Palmisano said.
That’s why IBM doesn’t have a hard time building its basics on many platforms – and when they don’t work, leave them.
Contrary to rival Microsoft, which basically stands and falls on the Windows operating system.
Perspective technology
IBM's revenues are mostly involved in services, after about a-fif-thort, they are made up of software and hardware.
Even in 1990, with more than half a share, it was the most possuing representative of the hardware.
Since 2000, IBM has shipped low-yielding $15 billion worth of low-yielding assets, investing $58 billion over the same time to buy prospective technologies.
Investiction has also continued since 2008, when a modern-day financial crisis swept through the world for the first time.
According to the legacy of its first boss, Thomas J. Watson, who also increased the amount of investment during the Great Depression.
So far, it seems that IBM is undergoing unspoiled in the current crisis.
Since the beginning of the year of 2008, IBM’s share prices have risen by 120 percent on a skyrocketing, and the company’s net profit has been rising continuously.
IBM's corporate motto is to change everything, it just doesn't.
Therefore, it can be expected that even if there is another crisis, this flexible giant can handle it.
IBM History: From Cheese Slicer to Space Flights
IBM (International Business Machines) originated in New York a hundred years a century ago and originally had the intricately name Computing Tabulating Recording Corporation.
It didn’t take the name IBM until 1924 until 1924 – it was originally a brand used for companies’ offices in Canada and South America.
The basis for the later IBM was given a fusion of four companies whose history dates back to the eighties of the nineteenth-century.
They possessed technologies, such as the not-so-familiatory "writters", i.e. hours recording the employee's arrival and departure.
The architect of the new company was businessman Charles Ranlett Flint, who also presided over the supervisory board of the company until 1930.
Flint has hired competitor CEO Thomas J. Watson to help him manage the company.
The leader then overshadowed the founders of IBM - Watson's thoughts are still built an invincible corporate culture and identity.
Watson led the company until 1952.
IBM, as its name suggests, began with the production and sale of all sorts of machines for business - from meat and cheese slicers to cockroaches.
In the first-in-four years that Watson was in charge of the company, the turnover doubled to nine-million-dollar dollars, and a large-scale expansion of the company into all continents began.
Watson was so indispensivable for the company that after almost forty years in the boss's chair, he was replaced by his son, Thomas Watson Junior.
Under the leadership of IBM began to work on the development of artificial intelligentsia, it has developed the first programming language.
In the 1960s, people and computers from IBM were helping NASA to control flights into space - Mercury, Saturn, and in 1969 the famous flight of man to the moon.
Thus, in 1964, IBM developed the first family of computers - the IBM System/360 series.
A classic "brée" that established a computer standard of that time, titled IBM 5150, came to the market in 1981.
Twenty years later, IBM released the production of computers of the Chinese company Lenovo, on the contrary, it bought the Consultative part of PricewaterhouseCoopers and began to fully devote herself entirely to advice and services with high added value.
A strategy that has been going on by IBM over the past three years - it's the Smarter Planet concept, "the smarter planets."
Its goal is the clever use of technologies in even unscheduled areas so far and improving the situation, for example, in transport or city management.
For the field of commerce, IBM has recently introduced the "Smarter Commerce" platform, which helps traders manage the entire commercial cycle.
IBM has a strong history in the Czech Republic as well.
She founded her branch in Czechoslovakia in 1932 as the first country in Central and Eastern Europe.
Today, in addition to the IBM Czech Republic, it also operates a strategic outsourcing center in Brno.
Headquarters for Central and Eastern Europe is headquartered in Prague and there is also a world-class world-class research team dealing with voice recognition.
Rychtář about an unfaithful husband:
Iveta, keep him, I don't want him anymore!
Darina Rychtářová (53) said the ending!
After her Husband Josef Rychtář (twin) became not only Iveta Bartoš's protector (45), but also a milief, Darina still hoped that Joseph would wake up from the pink dream and return home.
But now she doesn't want to wait and sets clear rules for the next life.
"Pepa can come home, but no longer as my partner," Rychtářová explained.
When Darina Rychtářová provided Bartoš’s asylum at her home in the summer, she probably didn’t even dream how her marriage would eventually end.
Even though Iveta moved away from Říčany after 30 days, Pepa didn’t abandon the singer.
He even publicly admitted that he loved her.
Over time, Darina resigned, reconciled with her husband's relationship, and now she even said goodbye to him forever.
Rychytarian doesn't care who his wife is sleeping with
If Rychtář and Bartošová broke up once after all after all, his wife's open arms will not await him at home.
"It's the biological father of my sons and if he wants to live up to his life in our shared house, no one will expel him."
"However, he will live to see it not as my beloved, straddled an old donkey, but as a person with whom I have certain ties," Rychtářová said, adding that she has already detached herself from her husband and insists only on mutual decency.
Joseph doesn't care that Darina's back door was closed yet.
"I respect the decision of my wife."
"With Iveta I won't, and I'm not going to change that."
"My wife has set up a paper marriage, and I respect that."
"The company goes on, I take care of repairs, garden, real estate, I shop."
"Doria and I'm talking quite normally, except that we don't share beds together," Rychtář told Blesk.
If Rychtářová also finds a new love, she says she wouldn’t stop her.
“We don’t sleep together and I don’t care where he’s going, who he’s going and if he has a boyfriend.
I know it's my fault, I fell in love with Iveta and I'm taking all my responsibility," Josef concluded.
