"Ununfortunately, statutes have been approved at the June General Meeting, which were not as perfect as everyone thought."
"Shouldn't concede various expositions, we've had a president since September," Pelta pointed out.
It was the reprocessing of the most important document of the Civic Association as a decolumn for delegates.
"If I'm going to become a chairman, I'm going to take it as a personal task, and I'm willing to take a personal responsibility if it doesn't happen."
