An exodus of customer's money.
Thus, over the course of a matter of several months, the bank lost its credibility in both central business areas: in investment banking due to misinterpreting speculations and in the management of assets for accusations of tax recovery.
And just when it calmed down a little again, just when it was thought that UBS had recovered again, this unfortunate business anabasis is coming: A single dealer wasted $1.7-billion-euro before the bank noticed that something was wrong.
And it's clear: it probably still doesn't seem to work out with risk management in investment banking.
“The Adoboli case may have probably been found to change too little,” says Martin Janssen, an Economist and Finanz Professor of Financing at Zürich’s Banking at the Zürich Universities.
The chief financial officer of a large German bank is also confident: "The UBS problem is that it does not cope with the control of risks."
After all, it was exactly the idea of the caution with which Swiss bankers started a long time ago in order to become guards of the great assets of the world: no too big risks, but security for money - even from this side, the world has collapsed the Alpine republic.
Vaults of the Swiss banks became a symbol for unshakable reliability such as Lindt and Sprüngli for particularly high-quality chocolate.
