In order to close the gap, UBS decided on an adventure that almost cost her existence.
Hunger-of-growth for growth has also been invested by both the bank itself and its based fund to secure risks in U.S. Subprime investments.
It developed into a massive machine that repackaged securities into U.S. Mortgage Loans and handed it over - but it also retained its own risks.
Also, when other banks searched for a long way off.
"Eillvent in the summer of 2007, when the real estate market was on fire, UBS was bought there," says banking expert Geiger.
How much euphoria is, such a deep fall.
