UBS positions have become a catapulting seat and to this day they are swinging.
Whoever runs a big bank now has an uncontrollable job.
They have to find a strategy for a bank that has vanished all nearby business models.
Geiger's banking expert already has an idea: An end to investment banking, concentrations on asset management, a return to Swiss roots.
The bank doesn’t want to go so far.
But investment banking is supposed to fall heavily, so much is now clear.
