SAP aims to redumpite the number of its employees in China.
The largest software maker in Europe SAP is investing billions in China in the coming years and wants to almost double the number of its employees in the country.
Around two billion dollars (approximately 1.5 billion euros), Dax said on Tuesday.
"We're going to set up additional research and development facilities, and we're going to employ relevant staff," Deputy CEO Bill McDermott said at a customer trade fair in Beijing.
The ositting is now expected to grow from 2500 employees to 4500.
