As a result, most words about pitimoration are uttered silently and privately between war veterans.
Retired colonel Mark Canciano's two sons returned from combat actions, where they served as nautical infantry members, their father warned them that people outside the army would look at their service from two angles.
From the point of view of some, they will feel respect and astonishment because they have defeated enemy insurgent insurgents and visited exotic places.
But others will wonder if there is an evil, violent veteran hiding under the surface," said Cancian, who participated in the fighting in Iraq and after his return took a seat in Washington in government.
