Bryan Ruiz has the most interventions on the Costa Rican side, nine, two more than Carlos Hernández and three more than Roy Myrie and Parks.
quintet included the country in its tour on the occasion of the celebration of twenty years of existence
"A journey to Costa Rica is a dream that comes true"
In an outspoken interview for Viva, bassist Jeff Ament from Pearl Jam said the group is ready to offer one of the best concerts at the National Stadium next Sunday.
We have been waiting for more than 20 years, but the group itself assures the fact that for them the opportunity to play in Costa Rica represents a dream come true.
This is what the bass bassist and founding member Jeff Ament, who interviewed Viva exclusively from Brazil last week.
The group is located on the South American continent as part of the tour on the occasion of the celebration of the twenty years of existence and will be at a unique stop in Central America on Sunday.
This day will perform from 19:30 a.m. at the National Stadium, along with the angel group The X and national musicians from Las Robertas.
This is an excerpt from an interview whose full transcript can be found on the La Nación website on the Internet.
It's a dream come true for your Costa Rican supporters. Pearl Jam will play in Costa Rica. Do you realize what your fans are experiencing?
The journey to Costa Rica is also our dream, which becomes a reality.
In South and Central America, we are hardly the second time and the experience so far has been great.
I've only been to Costa Rica once, on vacation. It's a beautiful country and I believe we're going to be able to stay here for a few days.
So we're very happy that we're going to bring you our music.
I ask, because they literally adore the group here, the fans experience these days of preparation very intensively.
What do you say to your most rocky supporters?
Thank you for standing with us for so many years.
It took us almost 21 years to get to Kostarika. Thank you for waiting so long and we are sorry that it took us so long.
Some people talk about the concert as the biggest show of the year.
Does it put more pressure on you?
Some of the biggest shows we've performed over the past 21 years have emerged within a few weeks.
We've done some great shows in Sao Paulo and we're hoping we've come into shape for a concert in Costa Rica.
We are really looking forward to the concert.
We love this country, we like to serfe, we like the jungle. For both activities, Costa Rica is the best country in the world.
How did you know Costa Rica and her waves suitable for surfing?
We've got a lot of surfers and I've got a good friend who resides in Tamamindo. The waves here are unbelievable.
My friends go surf to Costa Rica or Nicaragua or in Mexico. These are the best places to surf. And that's how we learned about Costa Rica, through people who love surfing.
Taking a look at your touring, you have prepared a huge show with many songs.
What have you planned for your presentation in Costa Rica?
Since we've never played here, we don't have any restrictions on what we couldn't.
We're going to try to perform the best possible show with a variety of songs. We're going to try to play a couple of songs from each album and introduce a good and diverse repertoire to our fans.
You'll never repeal the repertoire.
- Why ?
I don’t think it’s partly because we have nine albums and we can play more than 120 songs and everyone likes different songs, so it’s hard to choose which songs we’re going to play every night.
When we've had two-three songs we didn't play in the repertoire for a long time, we're concentricing and we're surprised because we're going to think about why we liked each other so much and that maybe we've already forgotten about it.
So the show is more interesting for us, and that's why I don't think it's more interesting for people.
With this tour you celebrate 20 years of artistic career.
When you look back, it's hard to believe everything you've done?
Yes, I'm sure.
First of all, I don't think any of us could have imagining that we're going to be in a big rock band and that we'd stay in it for more than 20 years.
We are aware of how much it has been given to us that we can continue to play with each other.
We love each other and like to create music.
We're lucky we can take a look at the places we've always longed for.
We couldn't have turned out better.
What did it mean to you that you were an important part of the grunge genre?
It has always been an acknowledgement for us that we can be a part of this group, in which all the greats are represented.
Soundgarden, Mudhoney and Alice in Chains are friends.
Surprisingly, when a movement arises from a group of guises, very often it does not happen.
From time to time a group arises in the city, but it is much less customary for five or ten groups to emerge from one city at the same time.
We're proud of it, and we're honored to be part of the Seattle group.
Sometimes we still play with some of them.
Last year we went to a festival with Alice in Chains and we were in Canada with Mudhoney, we saw Soundgarden on tour. We're lucky they're all our friends and we're honored to be a part of this movement that originated in Seattl.
Also, it's very impregnace for a group like yours to stay together and still have the same members after all these years.
Yes, the four of us have been together for 21 years and Matt (Cameron) joined us 13 years ago, which in itself is a much longer-a-half time than the usual duration of the group.
I don't really think we're all lucky, that we're still in this world, and the fact that we're constantly caring about each other plays a role.
We are all close friends and thanks to this we managed to unleash the musical paths, which leave everyone sufficient freedom for their own experimentation.
We trust each other, we appreciate each other's music and I don't think it could be better.
Your relationship with fame wasn't easy. However, thanks to your success, you can do what you like.
How do you find a balance?
As we grew, it gradually became more and more and easier to find a balance.
We try not to ride too much on tour, because it is very easy to fall into this trap of the crowds and people who love our music.
Recognizing that people came because of the music, you will remind yourself that you have to respect the music and what you gave it. You mustn't be kidnapped by the fact that you're faecic, rock stars. Neither of us has ever really really cared about this.
How do you remember the next Mother Love Bone project?
I think we've written great songs, and at the beginning it was something spectacular.
We've existed as a band for three years and we've never released an album after Andy (Andrew Woods died).
It was very frustrating, because it took so long. The most important thing is that even today we are friends with Bruce (Fairweather) and Greg (Gilmore), who started in the band with us. When I listen to a song or look at the photos, I remember Andy how unbelievable I laughed with him. It was always a joy to work with him, to laugh, to have fun.
She was an unbelievable person, and we're too short.
The national band Las Robertas will be tasked with starting a show in Costa Rica.
It's true that you're familiar with their work, especially Eddie Vedder, and that's why you've chosen them as an intruders?
Yes, the production sent us videos with several designs and we liked this group the most. That's why we're wondering what Las Robertas will offer live and they have to be very entertaining.
Why do you always respeal Yellow Ledbetter?
It's a question for Ed (Eddie Vedder), so I don't know.
He salutes it, and I think he adds the first thing he can think of.
Who Affects You as a Bassist?
Plenty of people.
Geezer Butler, John Entwistle, C. J. Ramone, John Doe, Paul McCartney, Chuck Dukowski.
There's so many that I could talk all night about bassists I like.
How did Pearl Jam keep grunge, although it is no longer in vogue?
I don't think we've all always felt a slight separation from the word grunge.
Speaking grunge, I'm imagine the groups I've referred to as Mudhoney, Soundgarden, Nirvana and everyone else that's created at the same time.
In the beginning, your music had a slightly gloomy character, and now it is more positive.
What's behind this change?
That's annoying because I've got the feeling that there's a few songs in the new album that's lighter, but there are also songs like The End or Juste Breathe, which are considered very gloomy, although they can sound positive.
For both of them, when Ed played them, I wept, and they're songs profoundly dark.
I don't think when you grow up and you've had some kind of trauma in your life, you're going to lose someone in your family or a quiver, these things begin to affect your art and music, and these two songs represent just that for me.
I also don't think you can be a happy person and still make gloomy musculoskelets.
Peru:
Fujimori was hospitalized again for medical tests
Former President Alberto Fujimori was hospitalized on Tuesday in a public hospital, where they will test him due to the muscular loss he suffers from the lower extremities, his attending physician reported.
A 72-year-old Fujimori who is serving a 25-year prison sentence for human rights viquities committed by his government (1990-2000) suffers from several illnesses, including language cancer, for which he has been operated on four times and is already in control by doctors.
MEP Alejandro Aguinaga, who is his personal physician, told Canal N television that Fujimori will undergo tests at the National Institute of Neo-Sculpable Illutical Illuminism within three days to find out why it hurts him and why he loses strength in his lower extremities.
Aguinaga has said that in his opinion, Fujimori could receive clemency for humanitarian reasons, however, the former president himself does not wish the pardon because he feels innocent.
He was operated four times due to tongue-cancinal cancer, he dropped 18 pounds, and other ailments like severe erosive gasthritis, a pancreatic cyst, kidney stones, high pressure and circulating problems in the legs, enumerated a doctor.
Fujimori has been serving a sentence since September 2007 in the National Directorate of Special Police Surgery.
In April 2009, he was sentenced to 25 years imprisonment for the death of 25 people who were stuntmen illegally in the early years of his government.
Mujica on a visit of Mexico to strengthen political ties
The official delegation, led by the Uruguayan president, José Mujica, accompanied by several ministers and businesswomen, will begin a visit to Mexico on Tuesday. Its aim is to achieve an expansion of trade between the two nations and to touch on the political issues of the region.
Mujica on Wednesday will meet her Mexican counterpart, Felipe Calderón. It is the most important meeting of a large-scale meeting full of meetings with representatives of politics, commerce, and representatives of the Uruguayan community living in Mexico. The program was published by the Uruguayan presidential office.
A meeting between the two presidents in Guadalajara will be used to exchure information on political issues between the two countries," the Uruguayan presidential office said.
According to the local media, Mujico will try to get Calderón to support Uruguay in a dispute with France, which occurred when French President Nicolas Sarkozy ranked the South American country on the list of tax havens at the G20 meeting in Cannes, France.
Sarkozy's speech has threatened that countries that will continue to remain as tax havens would be eliminated from the international community. This statement has provoked a dismissible position on the side of Uruguay and consultation with an ambassador to this European country.
Mexico presupposes the G20 since November. The G20 is a group made up of the world's most powerful emerging and evolved countries. With the Danuminated country, since January this year it has an agreement to exchange information to prevent double taxation.
In recent years, the Uruguayan government has been striving to speculate fiscal-exchanging agreements in order to come out of the "blacklist" of the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), to which there are countries that did not introduce all the required international standards of tax cooperation.
From a commercial point of view, Mexico and Uruguay have concluded the Free Trade Agreement (FTA) since 2004, thanks to which the exchange of goods between the two countries has been strengthened.
Bearded plumber runs in 3D thanks "Super Mario 3D Land"
For more than 25 years, Super Mario has relentlessly struggled to relentlessly to rescue Princess Peach from the clutches of a villain Bowser, but has never yet appeared in 3D: "Super Mario 3D Land" he will fight for the love of the girl with stereoscopic technology.
The title, which arrives this month in all stores around the world, has been formed from the beginning to take advantage of all the characteristics offered by the Nintendo 3DS portable console, which allows you to play three-dimensional games without having to wear glasses.
"Mario is a character who has to say how stereoscopy should work without goggles," said a print worker in Spain, Omar Álvarez while presenting a video game in Madrid.
Álvarez stated that "Super Mario 3D Land" is "The first Nintendo video game created specifically for this carrier" because up to this moment successful images such as "Star Fox 64 3D" or "Zelda: Ocarine of time 3D" were adaptations of already-existing titles.
In addition to the fact that "Super Mario 3D Land", "Super Mario 3D Land" is an "available" video game that makes it possible to harness a fast and smooth game.
Álvarez confirmed that "Super Mario 3D Land" contains two games in one: the first part is "similar", whose task is to attract less skilled users.
As soon as you surpass this level, you can embark on a "second round" at the levels of the game, which this time are more challenging.
In addition, users can choose the real time between "aggressive D" or one that only affects the depth of the action. But it will be necessary to play in 3D in order to overcome all sorts of challenges and "not succumb to optical deceptions".
It also envisages this new advent of Super Maria in 3D with the return of the character to the portable console, which has not happened since 2005.
In this video game, Nintendo plays into the note to those who watch the saga and repeat a successful formula from the previous episodes. It consists of the plumber of a bespoke man will have to go through dangerousminated platforms in order to free Princess Peach.
Although the player finds news in the movements, in the surroundings, in disguises and also among the enemies, there will also be an "playful" Luigi.
Colom Approves Portillo Extradition to the United States
President Álvaro Colom announced on Tuesday that he has taken action on the release of former President Alfons Portillo, which is to be held accountable in the United States for the purpose of laundering $70 million.
In this way, the process ended, which aimed for Guatemala to respond to the request of the northern country, which is requesting the extradition of Portillo, so that it could sanctify it.
At a press conference, Colom confirmed that his decision was in accordance with the indecisistance of the judiciary and the executive branch and that he bears in mind that the penal court has already ordered extradition.
Reassured that during his mandate he "didn't interfere" with the court's decisions and allowed all the extradition that came to his desk.
In Addition to Portillo, Sergio Ruano Marroquín will be extradited for homicide and grievous bodily harm and Edgar Estrada Morales and Víctor Estrada Paredes, both for drug trafficking.
Colom's move marks a step of execution after all judicial and constitutional instances have been exhausted to conduct a trial against a former president who ruled between 2000 and 2004.
Pursued in accordance with the Fifty Penal tribunal and the Constitutional tribunal (CC), Portillo will be extradited after his legal situation in Guatemala has been resolved and respect for human rights is guaranteed.
Portillo was reunited not guilty on embezzlement 120 million at the Ministry of Defense at the time of its presidency. This trial preceded extradition, but the Public Treasury rescinded and returned the case to the game.
Triniyev helped 6000 young in a state of threat
The organization was created to help uneducated children so that they do not find themselves on the fringes of society.
The balance of the first 25 years of the Trinijave social support organization is very important: 6,000 young people who were at risk of social executing have been helped. The organization has helped them overcome difficult situations for 25 years.
It is necessary to add one hundred jobs that have been acquired for this social group.
Yesterday's anniversary also served to present the balance sheet as part of the ceremonial act, which took place in the former production of the Fabra and Coats factories, which was attended by more than 300 people.
Trinijave originated at Trinitat Vella in 1986 to help young low-educated, jobless, drug addicts or when they could fall into social exclusion.
Yesterday's meeting in Sant Andrea was attended by a large number of representatives of organizations and institutions who have cooperated with the association over the past 25 years.
Divised political representation, at the time of the elections, showed the unified character of the work carried out by Triniyov.
Together with President Generalitat, Arture Mass, and his forerunner Jordi Pujol took part in the ceremonial act by a former Socialist Adviser for Education, Ernest Maragall, and former deputy mayor and current eco-socialist councillor Ricard Goma.
Both Fabra and Coats have also attended current Social Welfiser and Familiar Colossians, Josep Lluís Cleries, and Director-General for Social Work at La Caix, Jaume Lanaspa.
Mas said that Trinijave arose at a very difficult time, and that today's times also provide a number of obstacles, but he added that the work that the association has brought to this day "it is a good foundation."
The president cited Trinijave as an example of how it is possible to fight against adverse circumstances and how to deliver courage to people in difficult situations.
“Crigue is nothing new for this organization and for the work it does,” he said.
There has been an eviction of a taken-handed house where gigantic parties were held
Intruders applauded 11 out of 13 apartments in a building in Balmes, 51
12 occupiers left the house yesterday at noon without resisting
It all indications are that the nightmare experienced by the neighbors from the number 51 in Balmes Street is finally over.
Twelve people last noon voluntarily left the building they illegally inhabited and orchestrated gigantic parties that aroused their neighbors. They abandoned the building by order of the court and without having to interfere with the police.
At the end of the operation, the lock was exchanged on the dorm in order to prevent a repetition of the situation.
"Ofrom now on, the entry will be guarded," the warden said.
Occupiers, who seized 11 out of 13 apartments in a given building - the remnants are inhabited - they took away all the electrical and partially aquatic equipment, in addition, they painted the walls and left the garbage of all kinds, especially cans of alcoholic beverages.
Huge parties were held in the first three flats, which lasted for up to two days, waking other tenants.
In addition to the building there is a disco, Balmes 51, which has also been harmored.
Its owner, Maria Pantinat, explained to the Europa Press that as long as the building was occupied, sales fell by 80%.
The owner emphasizes that the occupiers of the building gave her unfair competition, because they sold drinks for 3 euros, while at a discotheque it costs 10.
In addition, the owner of the entertainment company had to respond to the lawsuits of the neighbours due to the noise. But the problems were not caused by visitors to the discotheque, but the residents of the occupied house and especially those who took part in the parties held here, whose frequency and intensity have increased in recent weeks, according to the agitated residents of the neighborhood.
The owner of the discos explained that the problems were so great that they even made a deal with the owner of the building and for nine months had forgiven her rent.
Municipal police have also confirmed that they have received more complaints from its neighbors in recent weeks about the situation.
Last week, the chairman of the People’s Party of the People’s Party at the town hall, Alberto Fernández Díaz, demanded that “the building be immediately evicted and put an end to the problems of civic cohabitation that the neighbors suffer from and the destruction of the area”.
The President of the People's Party explained that only one floor had been separated years ago, but in the last few months the occupiers have reached all the floors of the building and almost all the apartments, and in one of them there were even the thefts.
In this regard, he added that "it is necessary to put an end to impunity and to be consistent when it comes to deeds against civil responsibility that took place in the building".
Earlier yesterday, city police also cleared the building in Nou Barris.
At 15 o'crophazard police got into building 35 on Mont-ral Street after it was summoned by neighbors, who saw four people entering the building.
All four were immediately detained.
The park or the mountains ?
The architects met on the occasion of listing the procedure, which entails more than controversy regarding royalties
The 16-degree city tender again opens a debate over the role of Collserola Park in Barcelona.
In the mid-80's, at the age of greatest hey-bloom already defunct Corporación Metropolitana de Barcelona (CMB), this self-government printed several pamphlets in support of Collserola Park.
The flyer defined the mountain as a large park of metropolitan Barcelona.
What's more, it was supplemented by a numerical comparison with New York Central Park.
After CMB ceased to exist in 1987, the park returned to the minds of many as the upper border of Barcelona. The Catalan metropolis is one of the few that does not focus on the north-south axis, but up (hole) - down (sea).
Qualifying Collserola as a natural park goes in that direction.
The reference was no longer Central Park, but Yellowstone with wild boars instead of the Yogi bear.
Such was the position until September, when the town hall announced a mega-competition consisting of 16 auditions on the same number of entrance gates to Collserola.
The gate, of course, plays rather the idea of the park.
Either this, or someone's trying to put the gate in the field.
So there is only one question: Collserola, a park or a mountain?
During the competition, both from a purely organizational point of view and on the basis of a reflection on the city, this question becomes the central theme of all Barcelona architects.
It's already a theme as bitter as when the two members of this old caste have their hands at a meeting in an elevator.
And it was this act that provoked one of the rare coincidences between what three Barcelona architects and pre-adonate university professors think.
Miguel Roldán, Daniel Modol and Marta Bayon: the selection process has its justification.
According to Roldán, after the issue of the bay side began, "it is necessary" to also discuss the "mountain party", so Ildefons Cerd's speech about the green apples was not brought to an end.
"We have to build on the principle that Barcelona's largest park is the beach.
Among other things, its great accessibility.
Collserola is more complex", said the architect, for whom the name "government to Collserola" entails an "lexichological trap": we must not imagin "as entrances to the park, but rather as a demarcation of zones where it is possible to act".
Mododol, like Roldán and Bayona with the experience of the world of urbanism qualifies the proposal as an "intellectual challenge" providing "some dangers".
Danger resulting from the "uncerviousness presented to the project of a public place today" after the experience from the 80's, which had "its swan singing" in the area of the Forum.
The first concern is the delimitation of the boundaries where it should be built.
“To define something is to take the next step,” that is, in principle, to move a step further.
"It is necessary to bear in mind the new urban and planning tools, because the current ones (with reference to the Universal Metropolitan Plan (PGM)) can cause a real calamity."
If we focus in more detail on the question, Modol thinks that Collserola's valley slope can be "deemed as a park", but the Barcelon part does not for purely top-fognorous reasons.
Mododol also recalled that there is already a work carried out Patronat de Collserola, which "must not end up in the rubbish dump", although he welcomes the fact that the town hall offers his gremia to intervene in the project from "the first moment".
In addition, he understands the fact that the proximity of the mountain and the city is a kind of culprit that allows architects to participate in the debate, but "doubts", that it should be precisely this technical profile that will lead multidisciplinary teams ("it is all about the skills", he adds), which needs to be created: "Architectians should only be tools".
Bayona indicates that the answer to the question that gave the name of this game is complex, because in the basis for the selection process lacks a global vision Collserola: "There have been acquited 16 tenders that dealt with all the axis of the mountain-seater, but there is no longituitudinal study that would look at the area and understood it as a whole."
This causes at least him to sign up for all 16 tenders.
In other other time, the project of one gate can allude to the concept and the definition of an architect of the adjacent gate.
In his opinion, the town hall should guarantee that the zone located immediately above Ronda de Dalt should provide a full-length zone of equipment, which would ensure a smooth transition between the city and the greens.
Casino pardons Jonás Larrazábal who will be released
After 72 days of imprisonment, legal envoy Cadino Red parodied the mayor of Monterrey in a process in which he was prosecuted for alleged extortion.
Manuel Jonás Larrazábal spent 72 days in prison and will now be discharged after lawmaker Casino Red parodied him before the Second Criminal Court in a given precinct who was hearing an expulsion case in which the mayor of Monterrey's brother was inclashed.
After an assassination of Casino Royale, the owner of Casina Red, Sergio Gil García, posted a series of photos and videos on which Manuel Jonás was supposed to ask him to pay for an economic quota so that Monterrey City Hall would allow an illegal operation in a betting home.
After the public indictment, Prosecutor's Prosecutor's Office opened a criminal prosecutor's criminal prosecution. On September 2, he was detained and imprisoned for 30 days.
Then, after 4 hours spent in front of the Public Ministry's No. 3 Agent for Property Crimes, he was transported to Prison 1, located in Barrio Antiguo in the state's capital.
He remained there for the next 49 days after a second intrusive order was handed down and a Public Ministry agent refuted the possibility of complicity or organized crime.
On October 19, he was taken to a criminal court in Cadreyet on suspicion of extorcating Casin Red owners with one and a half-million peso. However, only a few hours remained in a mid-suboration prison because he was threatened with death.
The executives allowed him to stay in city-meablites de los Garza during the trial.
Jorge Yanáz was handcuffed an Arreviation order issued by the Secretary of the Second Crisis Court, Jorge Yanáz, who said that after nearly two months of investigation, sufficient evidence had been collected to prove Jonás’ guilt. The evidence includes, for example, the disbursement of $1.5 million peso to representatives of the casino in exchange for a promise that the operation would be allowed.
This Monday the legal envoy of Casina Red, Víctor Aldo García Gómez, came to Judge José Luis Pecin and applied for a pardon for the brother of the region's mayor. Based on this, he will soon be able to return to his freedom.
During a lawful hearing, a representative of the Public Ministry assigned to that court, Ramiro Arias, asked Garcia Gómez whether the damage had been rectified and which of the shareholders decided to pardon. However, the lawyer made it clear that the name would remain secret.
On the basis of an official file 19/7/2011, a legal pardon of Jonási Larrazábal is awarded. It will not be possible to file any complaint in the process that has been conducted against him. It is also not possible to apply for compensation for damages or punishment.
After reparation with the legal envoy around 15:50 a.m., the court ordered an immediate release of Larrazábal Bretón.
The secretor, Jorge Yanez, came to a prison in San Nicolás de los Garza to notify Jonás that he had been granted an official pardon and his case had been postponed into an archive.
He also informed him that the judge had issued an immediate order for his dismissal.
Secretary Dionisio Pérez Jácome presented the details of an aeronautical accident in which the governor's secretary, Francisco Blake, and seven others were killed.
The Secretariat for Communications and Transport (SCT) has reported that the results of an investigation into an accident in which government secretary Francisco Blake Mora was killed and seven others showed that the helicopter landed directly on the terrain with full force, without the pilot having a chance of attempting a forced landing.
Speaking at a press conference Dionisio Pérez Jácome, Secretary for Communications and Transport, said the pilot had stating before the start of the aircraft that the climatic flying conditions make it possible.
"The parts that appear suggest that the unit came into contact with the terrain several times, the wings were entangled in the branches of the trees 25 meters from the place where the unit lost its torso."
It also informed that the unit was intended for 19 people, therefore it met all the requirements for the transport of personnel.
In addition, he stated that on the basis of an investigation carried out in an area of impact, no parts were found on the ground.
"During the search it was found that parts of the aircraft were not located in a different place, so the plane crashed on the mainland as whole.
"The helicopter was intended for 19 persons, it met all the requirements for the transport of persons.
The terrain shows a slope with an inclination of seven-to-three degrees.
The secretary assured that at the moment it is the most important thing to obtain results as quickly as possible. However, an investigation can take several months or up to a year.
Gilberto López Meyer, director-in-a-general and auxiliary auxiliary services, declared that at the moment of the impact, the helicopter of the Presidential General Staff was moving at a cruise rate and the accident occurred on a soft up-and-elevation terrain.
"This information supports the hypothesis that at the time of the accident it was a common overflight operation," he said.
At a press conference, SCT Pérez Jácome enumerated six basic points of the investigation:
Visual flight:
In accordance with aeronautical standards, the flight was carried out according to the rules of the visual flight, that is, the garrison must be visible on the terrain during the flight.
Meteorological conditions:
The reports in AICM state adequate conditions at take-off, in accordance with the aircraft advances towards the border, between the DF and the State of Mexico there were noticeable lattice layers at low heights.
Elected routes:
It's arguably due to clouds, the crew was looking for a lower area and greater visibility up to Cuernavaca Valley.
Placing an impact.
Coordinators of the impact and the last helicopter footage from the radar coincide, it is probable that there was not a loss of control or disruption of the trajectory of the flight.
Dispersion of remnants in conficiated territory:
The information we currently have at our disposal allows us to assume that the impact occurred on a straight trajectory and from the side.
Execution of diffulgement of aircraft remnants indicates that at the time of the impact on the mainland the helicopter was celestial.
There was no fire or an explosion.
There was no evidence recorded at the scene of the accident to indicate that there was an explosion or a fire.
Receiod results of the investigation show that there may have been several contacts with the mainland.
During the off-road deterioratories of the aircraft were found at a height of up to 9,200 feet above the sea, the terrain sloping is sloping from seven to 30 degrees.
The photos show foothote, in which there was probably a decacation along the mentioned route.
The information provides elements that appear to indicate that the helicopter may have come into contact with the ground in several places.
After a careful search in the vicinity of the accident, in an area that is more extensive than the territory demarcation, the remnants of the helicopter have not been found, relieving the presumption that the impact took place in a state where the helicopter was still complete.
Mexican Health Insurance Institute Launches Gene Research That Causes Obesity
The Institute of Health Insured conducts research with the aim of discovering the gene responsible for the obesity of children and adolescents. The research is carried out with the support of experts from the IPN institute
The Mexican Institute of Health Insurance (IMSS) has announced that it is conducting research to reveal a gene that causes obesity in children and the young. The research called "The Genetics of Obesity in Children and Juveniles" will make it possible to obtain results related to overweight.
In a report, Miguel Cruz López, a senior Research Medical Squad in Biochemistry from the Specialized Hospital of the National Medical Center of the 21st Century, Miguel Cruz López explained that a multi-disciplinary team consisting of doctors, nurses, nutritionists and social workers had been constituted a multidisciplinary team.
This team relies on the support of specialists and gradgraduating students from the National Institute of Public Health (INSP) and from the Centre for Research and Advanced Studies (Cinvestava) of the National Polytechnic Institute (IPN).
The general public can also get involved in the research, which is entitled or unruly. People can come to the participants of IMSS sports centers in Valle de méxico, where juvenile tests will be carried out every other party from 8 a.m.
He emphasized that the research began in the Sports Center Cuauhtémoc (Mexic state) and from October 8 this activity has also been carried out at the Nezahualcoyolt Sports Center (Eareas of the Mexican state).
As soon as data is obtained from 500 to 600 children, the study will continue at the Independencia Sports Center (sother of the Federal Distrench) and eventually in the Morelos Sports Centre (norrheally from the Federal Center).
Explained that the aim of this research is to determine the components and importance of genetics when it comes to the development of obesity, and to trace risk factors on Mexican children and young people, thereby preventing the emergence of chronic degenerative diseases.
Regarding International Diabetes Day on November 14, he recalled that the aim is to collect data ranging from three thousand children and young people between the ages of six and 14 years of age, with the agreement and under the supervision of their parents, for the application of specific dietary questionnaires.
The questionnaire will also ask about physical activity and family history of hereditary diseases in order to evade risk factors, which could cause diseases such as diabetes or renal insufficiency.
He clarified that anthropometrometric measurements (calm, height, waist circumference are carried out to all participants every Saturday), blood pressure is measured, the level of glucose, triglicerds, cholesterol, insulin is determined, and genes are examined (trying to identify the genes that are involved in the development of pediatric obesity).
Cruz López has stated that the research reflects health workers' concerns over an errelling increase in children's weight.
'Health polls carried out between 1999 and 2006 showed that in just a six-year-on-teaching time there was a 77% increase in obeiacy for boys and 47% for girls. A dramatic surge also occurred in the case of overblowing', an IMSS expert said.
He stated that one of the reasons for finding indicators is the presumption that the population of the country differs from other populations by its genetic history.
Informed that the average Mexican has a 65% Indian-American-American genetic make-up, 30% European and 5% African. This fact is reflected in the genes that are responsible for the emergence of diabetes and overweight.
Explained that in general the genetics of obesity is commonly explained as an inability to incinerate the excess energy we consume (calories) and which is stored in the form of fats.
The researcher explained that the direct benefit of the participants lies in the fact that they will receive an overall assessment of the condition of the children, thereby ascertaining whether they show any known overweight or obsession.
He stated that even the presence of wrinkles of dark color (acanthosis) on the neck and forearm indicates the likelihood that the individual will suffer metabolic problems and pre-sugar conditions.
In the meantime, the information is confidential, doctors pass it on to their parents in writing, explaining all the measurements and lifestyle changes they have to carry out in order for their children to avoid the disease.
Cruz López explained that there are three main components that cause overweight, obesity and other chronic diseases: a sedentary way of a life signifying a lack of daily physical activity, all-day sitting in front of the television, and the use of means of transport instead of walking short distances.
Oversucitism also causes great caloric intake, i.e. greater consumption of sweetened beverages, carbohydrates (tamalas, bread, pizza, hamburgers, etc.) with a high content of fats and proteins, and the genetic burden that is the subject of this research.
There won't be a Potholes in Asphalt from UNAM
Rafael Herrera, a scientist from the Faculty of Chemistry of UNAM creates modified asphalt with polymers, thus creating a mixture with better functionality, regardless of climatic conditions and temperature
If paving were properly cared, it would not be necessary to repair almost 200 thousand potholes after each rainy season in the metropolitan area of Valle de México, Rafael Herrera Nájera, a scientist from the Faculty of Chemical Technology (FQ) from UNAM, who at the same time added that if the construction and maintenance of asphaphalt pavements were adequate, there would have been a significant reduction in potholes, or it would even be possible to remove them completely.
In his quotation The Technological Caution of Potholes he uttered as part of the International Year of Chemistry, he announced that the laboratory under its leadership was developing modified asphalt with polymers, which should create a mixture with similar characteristics as asphalt, but at greater mechanical resistance, both at low-temperature and at high temperatures.
Herrera Najera believes that this kind of modified asphalt could be used in places with an extremely warm climax, for example, in some towns in the north of the country. It would improve functionality and reduce the formation of potholes.
Explained that asphalt, the heaviest part of crude oil, is a grouping of hydrocarbon molecules, molecules with high molecular weight that are called asphaltones, and others with low molecular weight that are called maltens. Together, they give asphalt a typical viscoelastic character.
Viscoelastic asphalt character lies in the fact that at high temperatures, around 180 degrees, it behaves like a liquid, has a high viscosity at 120 degrees, and at 50 degrees it is almost in a solid state, while at low temperatures the asphalt tends to break, he added.
This means the resilience of asphalt in the streets is unified, but it varies during the day according to meteorological conditions and temperature, the chemical engineering expert pointed out.
A Scientist from the Faculty of Chemistry has observed the fact that most of the streets in the Ciudad de México are covered with flexible pavement consisting of six layers of materials, three of which are mixed with asphalt.
There is an asphaphalt insert between the outermost layers, consisting of small stones embedded in asphalt and then compressed.
He emphasized that every stone that forms a liner is pouched with asphalt.
It is thus possible that the forces in the pavement decompose well when passing through or when creating pressure.
If it were a modified asphalt, they would decompose even better, the chemical engineer thinks.
He added that on an asphalt liner there will be the last layer called a cloak, consisting of fine stones, i.e. sand also poured in asphalt asphalt.
Since this layer comes into contact with vehicle rims, it must have a greater mechanical force than an asphalt liner and must ensure road friction.
Due to the fact that, as part of the paving, it will be subjected to a large load, it must have a sufficient thickness and it must be taken to pay attention to the material from which it is made.
Clima, especially moisture and temperature changes, are also a very important factor that needs to be borne in mind. In particular, water has a great effect on the functionality of the asphalt liner.
As soon as the terrain is moist, the water spreads in and it is difficult to get out, this causes softening of all layers of the pavement and thus the formation of potholes.
Explained that during the creation of potholes, the cassage film is the first to be devastated, and only then there is damage to the asphalt liner. However, the damage does not occur at the same moment, but it is a gradual process, which should be stopped already at the first signs with the help of appropriate maintenance programs.
As a member of the National System of Scientists, he also explained that the load of vehicles is another important factor in the creation of potholes, and therefore the thickness of each individual layer of paving must correspond to the load of vehicles and it must be guaranteed that this burden will not be exceeded. Only in this way we can prevent the frequent occurrence of potholes.
Rafael Herrera pointed out that when it comes to asphalt, we still have a lot of work to do, and the research is at the outset. It is worth noting, for example, asphalt emulsions, which are already available on the market in other countries and make it possible to easily repair potholes without having to use high temperatures.
