After all, Moleskine, as we know it today, was born in 1997.
At the same time the Italian company Modo Modo Headquartered in Milan decides to put on the market a new design but dissuded notebook.
Maria Sebregondi, then a consultant working for the company, takes on the introduction of a new product.
Inspired by "meleskin" (hisnia immitation), which, for example, is used for the treatment of the surface of the benches.
This type of notebook was highly valued by writers and travelers.
“Maleskine returned an old andforgosforned object that was an icon of avant-garde artists until the 20th century,” says Maria Sebregondi, who has since become a leading brand at Modo Modo Modo.
The success is here.
Between 2006 and 2010, sales rose by 26% in order to settle at 12.7-hundred-metre last year.
The Situation is far from classified production from the first years, when only 3 000 notebooks were made.
Moleskine crosses the Italian border and exports to 70 countries from France to the United States.
Difficulty compulsoring an artificial portrayal of the buyer, because the notebook impresses a businessman in the same way as a student or professionals.
Moleskine's image is that its owners are cosmopolitan, cultivated and open spirit.
The small Italian company, which had 12 employees in its early days, now has almost a hundred of them and since 2008 it has two offices, one of which is in Milan and the other in New York.
He sends his notebooks to a bookstore and through the FNAC store chain to small boutiques in the centers of the cities, where he was able to assert his identity.
“We followed the spirit of the times and this need for new writing, through the tumultuous development of e-mails,” explains Maria Sebregondi.
This cultural signature accompanies the development of the Moleskine notebook: the brand has recently opened an exhibition " Zacházka", where architects or artists exhibit their notebook.
